<title>UK: Imperial,Gallaher like court ruling.</title>
<headline>Imperial,Gallaher like court ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The two British tobacco firms that are being sued by 47 smokers welcomed a High Court decision on Friday not to assign a trial judge to the case.</p>
<p>The lawyer for the plaintiffs, Martyn Day, earlier welcomed the appointment of judge Anthony May during a closed-door hearing to handle the preliminary stages of the case.</p>
<p>But Imperial Tobacco Group Plc said it was pleased that the hearing was &quot;nothing more than a very preliminary administrative step in the legal process. It has nothing to do with the merits of the case and it dealt exclusively with the question of how the litigation is to be handled.&quot;</p>
</text>
